VERDICT.  The Myrheim-Meyer estimator cleanly separates the two families:
  - SPRINKLED (manifold-like): r ~ f(d), d_MM recovers the embedding dimension (2d->~2, 3d->~3).
  - KR-type RANDOM (non-manifold): height-2, r off the manifold curve, d_MM tracks NO embedding
    dimension; and these orders DOMINATE the uniform measure (n^2/4 exponent).
  => Manifold-likeness is the gate Malament(order->conformal)/BHS/Paper VII presuppose, and the
     uniform measure is dominated by non-manifold orders (the dominance/entropy problem). The
     causal order ALONE does not select a manifold; a DYNAMICS (selection rule) is required --
     the open core of the entire causal-set program. SHARD inherits this wall (not SHARD-specific).
